{
  "$schema-note": "One document per row of the silent-loss table in docs/test-findings.md, with the note that row must produce. Read by src/features/registry/lossCorpus.test.ts, which runs every case and DERIVES the verdict rather than reading one. A case whose note fires is `lossy, told`; a case whose note does not fire is `lossy, silent`; a row with `input: null` is `not verified`. Most of this file is red on the day it lands, and that is the point: a ratio has a denominator, and a denominator is a thing somebody can add to.",
  "howToAddACase": "Append an object with the next `row` number, a unique `id`, the `tool` and `options` that reproduce it, an `input` that loses something, a `clean` input of the same shape that does not, and the `expect` the note must satisfy. Nothing else has to change: the test derives the table and the ratio, and the doc block it writes into docs/conversion-matrix.md is compared rather than maintained.",
  "roundsThatReportedZero": [
    {
      "reported": "round three",
      "foundBy": "round four",
      "found": 2
    },
    {
      "reported": "rounds four to seven",
      "foundBy": "round eight",
      "found": 17
    }
  ],
